# Effects — Visual Node Editor for GPU Image Pipelines

## What This Is

A browser-based visual node editor for building GPU image-effect pipelines. Users create processing graphs by wiring nodes on a React Flow canvas; each node is backed by a **processor** that runs shader / compute logic via PixiJS (WebGL2) and publishes typed outputs downstream. The engine executes the entire graph every frame in topological order, enabling real-time preview of multi-pass shader effects, depth estimation, segmentation, contour extraction, and animation.

The app is a single-page tool — there is one route (`/`) that renders the `NodeEditor`.

