## UI Architecture

### NodeEditor.tsx (~280 lines)

Orchestrates everything: `useNodesState` + `useEdgesState` (React Flow), `engineRef` (DataflowEngine), four custom hooks, toolbar, sidebar, context menu. Loading gate shows "Initializing GPU..." until Pixi is ready.

### BaseNodeShell.tsx

Wraps every node view. Renders: `NodeResizer` (visible when selected, grid-snapped), coloured header (accent from category via CSS `--pn-accent`), input/output `<Handle>`s at 20px row pitch (aligned to editor grid), widget area, pin toggle button.

Two modes: **graph** (full chrome + handles) and **headless** (no handles/resizer — used in pin sidebar).

### EditableStepEdge.tsx (383 lines)

Custom orthogonal edge with draggable bend points. Segments snap to grid. Bend data persists in `edge.data.bends`. Supports selection, deletion, and hover states.

### Node Views (`views/`)

29 components, one per processor type. Each wraps `BaseNodeShell` and renders parameter widgets using the `widgets/` components. They access the engine via `useEngine()` and update params via `useSetParam()`.

### Category Colours

10 distinct hues with intentional progression: green (input) → gold/orange/pink (animation chain) → blue (image ops) → teal (contour) → sky (depth) → violet (AI) → red (output) → slate (util). All dark enough for white header text readability.

